      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. Looking at it more detailed, some of the table alterations just add *nullable* new columns https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/btservice/storage/MetadataDatabase.java. These do not need to be added to the ContentValues device object and are usually checked only for the columns existence with a null value such as:\n\u003e `assertColumnBlobData(cursor, \"spatial_audio\", null);`\n\nCompared to the other fields such `active_audio_device_policy` which are marked `NOT NULL` and must be filed in for the test to pass.\n\nI thought of reusing `contentValuesDevice_116()` for both `testDatabaseMigration_116_117()` and `testDatabaseMigration_117_118()` but to keep a convention of 1 test with 1 contentValues function, I decided to keep the 1:1 ratio with these single line functions. PLMK if you think it\u0027s better to reuse if there are no changes in the ContentValues device object.",
